Tijuana when my dad was performing.


01:32:41.890 --> 01:32:44.159
It's a picture of him in his
mariachi outfit, right?


01:32:44.259 --> 01:32:45.293
And he's got the microphone,


01:32:45.393 --> 01:32:49.130
and my mom is sitting front row
center with a white miniskirt on.


01:32:49.230 --> 01:32:52.000
And she's got her hand like this,
and she's looking at my dad,


01:32:52.100 --> 01:32:56.704
and she has this look on her face like,
"We're going to make a Fluffy."


01:33:08.183 --> 01:33:11.353
I never framed it. I keep
it at home in a drawer.


01:33:11.453 --> 01:33:13.989
It's weird for me to look at
the picture on a regular basis,


01:33:14.089 --> 01:33:15.790
so I keep it in a
folder in my drawer.


01:33:15.890 --> 01:33:17.359
Every now and then,
I'll open it, take a look at it.


01:33:17.459 --> 01:33:20.071
I'm like, "All right.
It's cool." It'll make me smile.


01:33:20.562 --> 01:33:22.831
Here's what I was
talking about earlier


01:33:22.931 --> 01:33:27.102
about the whole parallels
with my son and with me.


01:33:27.435 --> 01:33:31.339
As this whole situation's going on,
where my dad comes back into my life,


01:33:31.439 --> 01:33:36.111
Frankie's dad comes back into
his life at the exact same time.


01:33:36.211 --> 01:33:38.613
And for me, you guys,
this was way more upsetting


01:33:38.713 --> 01:33:40.715
than the whole situation with my dad.


01:33:40.815 --> 01:33:42.951
This guy e-mails me, right?
He had my e-mail address.


01:33:43.051 --> 01:33:45.120
And of course,
now he decides to use it.


01:33:45.220 --> 01:33:47.188
And I recognized the
name as soon as I saw it.


01:33:47.288 --> 01:33:48.456
And then I opened up the e-mail,


01:33:48.556 --> 01:33:51.192
and right away, "I want to
thank you for raising Frankie.


01:33:51.292 --> 01:33:52.994
"I want to thank you for
being there for Frankie.


01:33:53.094 --> 01:33:54.796
"I want to be involved
in Frankie's life.


01:33:54.896 --> 01:33:56.831
"I want to take him to sports.
I want to get involved.


01:33:56.931 --> 01:33:58.233
"I want to be there
for him financially..."


01:33:58.333 --> 01:34:00.535
And I'm getting pissed.
I'm getting piss...


01:34:00.635 --> 01:34:03.638
I'm screaming again. I'm like, "Really?
Now you want to get involved?


01:34:03.738 --> 01:34:05.473
"Now you want to be a part of this,


01:34:05.573 --> 01:34:07.242
"after all the love
and time and energy


01:34:07.342 --> 01:34:10.378
"I put into a kid that wasn't even mine?
Are you shitting me?


01:34:10.478 --> 01:34:12.954
"I just got him to
take out the trash."


01:34:16.251 --> 01:34:19.387
I started yelling at the screen more,
and my girl hears me, so she comes in.


01:34:19.487 --> 01:34:20.488
She goes, "What's going on? Relax."


01:34:20.588 --> 01:34:22.257
I go, "Look at the screen.
Look at the screen."


01:34:22.357 --> 01:34:26.227
"What? Relax." "Look at the screen."
"Calm down." So she starts reading.


01:34:26.327 --> 01:34:28.229
And as soon as she starts
reading, she starts,


01:34:28.329 --> 01:34:29.898
"Oh, this asshole,
now he's going to ruin every..."


01:34:29.998 --> 01:34:31.566
And now I got to be her rock.


01:34:31.666 --> 01:34:34.312
So I stand up, and I'm like,
"No, it's okay. Shh..."


01:34:35.103 --> 01:34:36.646
"But he's going to..."


01:34:37.705 --> 01:34:40.008
Frankie hears his mom
getting hysterical,


01:34:40.108 --> 01:34:44.946
and then he walks into the office,
and he's like, "Who died? Who died?"


01:34:45.046 --> 01:34:47.549
I go, "No, Frankie, nobody died.
Get in here." "Why is my mom crying?"


01:34:47.649 --> 01:34:49.451
"I'm going to tell you why your
mom's crying. Have a seat."


01:34:49.551 --> 01:34:51.419
"I'm in trouble, huh?"
"Frankie, you're not in trouble."


01:34:51.519 --> 01:34:54.325
"I didn't do it. "Whatever it is,
you did it. Sit down."


01:34:56.658 --> 01:34:58.026
So he sits down.


01:34:58.126 --> 01:35:00.895
I got these office chairs
with the little wheels, right?


01:35:00.995 --> 01:35:02.030
And so I sit down.


01:35:02.130 --> 01:35:04.399
He sits in front of me, and I
sit his mom down next to me,


01:35:04.499 --> 01:35:06.968
and I grab his chair, and I
pull it right up to mine.


01:35:07.068 --> 01:35:08.436
And his knees are pretty
much touching mine,


01:35:08.536 --> 01:35:10.805
and he's right here,
and I go, "Listen, Frankie,


01:35:10.905 --> 01:35:12.774
"what I got to tell you
is probably the hardest


01:35:12.874 --> 01:35:15.452
"thing I've ever had
to say to you. Um...


01:35:16.244 --> 01:35:18.117
"Your dad...


01:35:18.346 --> 01:35:21.549
"Your dad, he...
Your dad wants to see you."


01:35:21.649 --> 01:35:23.692
And he looks at me, and he goes...


01:35:24.652 --> 01:35:26.229
"I'm right here."


01:35:28.890 --> 01:35:30.296
Oh.


01:35:46.374 --> 01:35:49.110
I go, "Frankie, I love you so much,
but that's not what I mean.


01:35:49.210 --> 01:35:52.254
"Oh, my God! Your dad-dad."


01:35:53.047 --> 01:35:54.582
"Dad-dad?"


01:35:54.682 --> 01:35:57.085
"Oh, my God. Um...


01:35:57.185 --> 01:35:59.126
"The man that gave you life?"


01:36:00.922 --> 01:36:02.567
"Jesus?"


01:36:03.458 --> 01:36:07.401
"No! Oh, my God! That's my dad.


01:36:14.569 --> 01:36:17.372
"Your biological father,
Frankie. Your dad.


01:36:17.472 --> 01:36:21.745
"Your mom's ex-boyfriend,
your father, your dad, Randy."


01:36:22.710 --> 01:36:25.847
And he went from having
this look of confusion


01:36:25.947 --> 01:36:27.982
to, like, a straight-up
despaired look.


01:36:28.082 --> 01:36:30.185
He just looks at the ground,
and he starts mumbling.


01:36:30.285 --> 01:36:34.355
And as soon as he finished mumbling,
he starts telling me his memory,


01:36:34.455 --> 01:36:37.792
his last memory of his dad.
And I'll be honest with you guys.


01:36:37.892 --> 01:36:40.361
It's one thing to hear a
messed-up story involving a kid


01:36:40.461 --> 01:36:42.997
seeing something he shouldn't
have seen from an adult.


01:36:43.097 --> 01:36:46.201
It's another when you hear
it from the kid themselves.


01:36:46.301 --> 01:36:47.669
And so for me, I'm just like,
"Oh, my God!


01:36:47.769 --> 01:36:49.137
"Why am I putting him through this?"


01:36:49.237 --> 01:36:51.306
He starts telling me,
and my girl is just bawling.


01:36:51.406 --> 01:36:52.974
I'm getting choked up.
I go, "Look, Frankie,


01:36:53.074 --> 01:36:55.076
"whatever you want to do,
okay, we support it.


01:36:55.176 --> 01:36:57.478
"If you want to see your dad,
your mom and I will make it happen.


01:36:57.578 --> 01:36:59.480
"If you don't want to see him,
you don't have to see him,


01:36:59.580 --> 01:37:02.050
"but you're old enough now,
and it has to come from you.


01:37:02.150 --> 01:37:03.651
"So you let us know
whenever you're ready,


01:37:03.751 --> 01:37:05.753
"and we'll make it
happen either way."


01:37:05.853 --> 01:37:08.990
"What do you think I should do?"
"Frankie, I wish I could tell you.


01:37:09.090 --> 01:37:10.592
"I wish I could tell you, honestly,


01:37:10.692 --> 01:37:13.428
"but you saw what I just went through."
You were yelling at the mirror."


01:37:13.528 --> 01:37:16.732
"I know I was yelling
at the mirror. I know."


01:37:17.632 --> 01:37:20.268
"What did you do?" "Well, Frankie,
in my case, it was different,


01:37:20.368 --> 01:37:23.871
"because my dad waited 30 years,
and so I had to wait 30 years,


01:37:23.971 --> 01:37:27.342
"and fortunately for me,
I was more mature,


01:37:27.442 --> 01:37:29.611
"and I was able to handle
it a little bit better.


01:37:29.711 --> 01:37:31.512
"Plus your mom was there
to keep me in check,


01:37:31.612 --> 01:37:34.182
"so I didn't do anything
stupid, but 30 years,


01:37:34.282 --> 01:37:37.552
"it actually worked out pretty good,
and now we have an actual...


01:37:37.652 --> 01:37:39.887
"We're going to go back and
forth and start talking,


01:37:39.987 --> 01:37:42.056
"so 30 years worked out for me."


01:37:42.156 --> 01:37:44.592
And then he looks at the ground,


01:37:44.692 --> 01:37:48.062
and it felt like it took forever.
I wanted to ask him if he was okay,


01:37:48.162 --> 01:37:50.231
but I didn't want to accidentally
trigger another memory


01:37:50.331 --> 01:37:52.367
and put him through that same
thing again, so I'm just waiting,


01:37:52.467 --> 01:37:54.035
and his mom's wailing,
and we're just waiting,


01:37:54.135 --> 01:37:57.712
and then he looks at me,
and he goes, "You know what?


01:38:00.975 --> 01:38:03.018
"I'm gonna wait 30 years, too."


01:38:06.881 --> 01:38:08.788
Oh, my God!


01:38:10.318 --> 01:38:11.786
I got so choked up.


01:38:11.886 --> 01:38:14.088
I started crying, and then he
puts his hand on my shoulder,


01:38:14.188 --> 01:38:15.823
and I started bawling.


01:38:15.923 --> 01:38:18.393
And then he hugs me,
and I'm like, "Oh, my God!"


01:38:18.493 --> 01:38:19.761
And we're hugging, and I'm crying,


01:38:19.861 --> 01:38:21.929
and his mom's crying,
and then she looks at me.


01:38:22.029 --> 01:38:27.335
"Now what are you gonna do?
Now what are you gonna do?"


01:38:27.435 --> 01:38:29.570
"What do you think I'm gonna do?


01:38:29.670 --> 01:38:31.747
"I'm going to get him an iPhone."


01:38:37.779 --> 01:38:39.720
Thank you, Bay Area.


01:38:40.114 --> 01:38:43.158
I love you guys. Thank you.


01:41:37.124 --> 01:41:38.894
Hijo, I'm home.


01:41:39.727 --> 01:41:41.262
Did you give any more
thought to my question


01:41:41.362 --> 01:41:44.230
about what you want to
